# Build context for every image is the repository root; all Dockerfile paths are
# repo-relative. Everything is excluded by default, re-included explicitly.
#
# The leading `*` is what keeps artifacts/ out. The context is hashed and
# transferred on every build; the 950PR archive alone is 3.1 GB.
# See docs/repository-layout.md.
*

# Offline payload. Bind-mounted at build time, never COPYed.
!deps

# Not read by any Dockerfile. The vLLM checkout exists only so provisioning can
# build its wheel; .provision is scratch; src tarballs are delivery vehicles for
# trees extracted beside them.
deps/src/vllm
deps/.provision
deps/950pr-x86_64/src/vllm
deps/950pr-x86_64/src/*.tar.gz

# Image assets: Dockerfiles, entrypoints, verify suites, package lists,
# constraints, container-side provisioning scripts.
!docker

# Final deployable archives. Redundant while `*` stands; explicit so a later
# broad re-include cannot expose them.
artifacts
artifacts/**
*.tar.gz
